Hi Jon,
The easiest thing to do is to look at the output of the logs.  You can do that by running shinyapps::showLogs() or by looking at the logs tab in the Application tab within the shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> dashboard.
In this case, I can see the error.  You have a setwd() call that is an absolute path, you can't do that with shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>.  You need to have the directory that has the content you are loading within the directory structure of the application itself and you can then refer to it with relative paths.

Hope this helps.
-Tareef

